# Command: SDD Backup

Command: /sdd-backup
Mode: READ_ONLY
Purpose: Create timestamped backup of critical .sdd/ files

Description:
  Creates a backup of critical .sdd/ files to .runtime/backup/.
  Backup includes file hashes for integrity verification.
  Old backups are rotated (keeps last 10).

Usage:
  /sdd-backup
  /sdd-backup --name=<backup-name>
  /sdd-backup --list

Options:
  --name=<name>   Custom backup name (default: timestamp)
  --list          List existing backups
  --rotate        Rotate old backups (keep last 10)

Backup Location:
  .runtime/backup/
    YYYY-MM-DDTHH-MM-SZ/
      PROJECT.sdd
      INDEX.sdd
      ROOT.sdd
      graph.sdd
      templates/INDEX.sdd
      manifest.json

Backup Manifest:
  {
    "timestamp": "2026-08-28T10:00:00Z",
    "files": [
      {
        "path": ".sdd/PROJECT.sdd",
        "hash": "sha256:...",
        "size": 1234
      }
    ],
    "system_version": "1.0.0"
  }

Backup Policy:
  [B1] Auto-backup before any modification to critical files
  [B2] Keep last 10 backups (rotation)
  [B3] Backup includes file hash for integrity verification
  [B4] Backup manifest tracks timestamp, file list, and hashes

Rotation:
  - Keep last 10 backups
  - Delete oldest when limit exceeded
  - Archive old backups to .runtime/archive/ (optional)

Exit Codes:
  0 - Backup successful
  1 - Backup failed
  2 - No critical files found

State: +
